{{- /*
The text arm. It is not a fallback — it is REQUIRED on every message, and
mailer.render only emits multipart/alternative when both arms exist. A
transactional mail that only renders as HTML is unreadable in a client
configured to refuse it, and those clients are common exactly among the people
most likely to be running a self-hosted instance.

The action URL is written out in full rather than hidden behind link text: there
is nowhere to hide it here, and a bare URL is also what lets someone verify the
host before clicking.
*/ -}}

{{- /*
The text arm mirrors the HTML arm's three shapes, and that is a correction
rather than symmetry for its own sake.

It used to be ONE layout with optional slots — `{{ with .ActionURL }}`,
`{{ with .Code }}` — while the HTML side had already been split so that a notice
message has nowhere to put a link. The result was a guarantee that held on half
the wire format: rendering session_revoked with an injected ActionURL printed
the raw URL, under a stray empty-label colon, two lines above the footnote
promising the message carries no link. Every text client auto-linkifies a bare
https://, and a reader who refuses HTML sees only this arm. The Code slot leaked
the same way.

Gating each slot on its own field was tried and rejected: it fixes whichever
field you thought of, and the first attempt gated the URL and left the Code
leaking. THE SHAPE IS THE GUARANTEE — a form with no slot cannot leak one it
does not have. The `with .Action` on the action shape below is not part of that
guarantee (by then the shape has already decided); it only keeps a message whose
copy defines no label from printing a bare colon above its URL.

There is no styling to differentiate here, so all eleven live in this file
rather than in eleven near-identical ones. The shape is therefore declared
twice — once here, once in the message's .html.tmpl — and what makes that safe
is TestLinklessMessagesCannotBeGivenALink, which injects both an ActionURL and a
Code into every notice message, in every locale, and checks BOTH arms.
*/ -}}

{{- define "text.shape_action" -}}
{{ .Heading }}
{{ range .Body }}
{{ . }}
{{ end }}
{{- with .Action }}
{{ . }}:
{{ $.ActionURL }}
{{ end }}
{{- template "text.close" . }}
{{- end -}}

{{- define "text.shape_code" -}}
{{ .Heading }}

    {{ .Code }}
{{ range .Body }}
{{ . }}
{{ end }}
{{- template "text.close" . }}
{{- end -}}

{{- /* No URL slot and no code slot. Do NOT add either. */ -}}
{{- define "text.shape_notice" -}}
{{ .Heading }}
{{ range .Body }}
{{ . }}
{{ end }}
{{- template "text.close" . }}
{{- end -}}

{{- define "text.close" -}}
{{- with .Footnote }}
--
{{ . }}
{{ end -}}
{{- with .Footer }}
{{ . }}
{{ end -}}
{{- end -}}

{{- define "text.invite" -}}{{ template "text.shape_action" . }}{{- end -}}

{{- define "text.password_reset" -}}{{ template "text.shape_action" . }}{{- end -}}

{{- define "text.verify_email" -}}{{ template "text.shape_action" . }}{{- end -}}

{{- define "text.admin_recovery" -}}{{ template "text.shape_action" . }}{{- end -}}

{{- define "text.login_code" -}}{{ template "text.shape_code" . }}{{- end -}}

{{- define "text.enroll_email_2fa" -}}{{ template "text.shape_code" . }}{{- end -}}

{{- define "text.step_up_code" -}}{{ template "text.shape_code" . }}{{- end -}}

{{- define "text.reset_unavailable" -}}{{ template "text.shape_notice" . }}{{- end -}}

